{"skill":{"slug":"listenhub-ai","displayName":"ListenHub"},"version":{"version":"0.6.0","createdAt":1772330875509,"changelog":"Initial OpenClaw adaptation from marswaveai/skills. Podcast, explainer video, TTS, speech, and image generation via ListenHub API.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":5183,"sha256":"be129afc6a9b3a1b2b4e0867003062218879e8f06ef60932bbcce786983f922f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/check-status.sh","size":3905,"sha256":"f088c8c8fd8d079d6832e707e22c954b34662fe1157f73b9b41a33d722f59b93","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/create-explainer.sh","size":2115,"sha256":"52e634357ff02a3edd309df2f352f9a16799759998d7b38e35004ba692d45768","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/create-podcast-audio.sh","size":2418,"sha256":"914c08d7b4d181dd8671ee27d1043983b48fa7655041056d6c4c978b2a6d70c4","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/create-podcast-text.sh","size":4456,"sha256":"8d43d8883b564959513eb86bceee071be85b1171f12a0b534e896b1455ffc02c","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/create-podcast.sh","size":4578,"sha256":"45be45592e2666f6197f5a93632140a769d76cedd969d4a13f07e08e8b02556c","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/create-speech.sh","size":2047,"sha256":"3dd8f2cc7255c64ade63617b5cf36b8ce856404c30fffd090957ef5aeb52af6a","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/create-tts.sh","size":3077,"sha256":"fbd05a66abc7aed353513e8c6550ac04b52f0b92c289051a0a85f37e99c6c7e1","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/generate-image.sh","size":21759,"sha256":"69e5cabee7b7999557b37d3db1c8597f693ecfa93d227755025a45395a995e55","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/generate-video.sh","size":716,"sha256":"120d299606c5b97eb7ff67eadf8fc9a376f92f5e059c541ab43122bf852ee126","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/get-speakers.sh","size":737,"sha256":"de514f63b486995d696a43b7784693e0633ed392594f65a472685a60e35ea178","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/lib.sh","size":6003,"sha256":"8f2b12230a912c180b31a564d654fda6e433885e6f8c8b86e7b1252f662c1281","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2695,"sha256":"9bc28c85e0663fb36979a02646dbab42d51140d5b2f0d4ab78c3b4d89c7c0f34","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789093231482,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"a49a13d20bb0b0567791894f562062856a29cd21a7c7025e34dcc2b7c82b1741","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/a49a13d20bb0b0567791894f562062856a29cd21a7c7025e34dcc2b7c82b1741","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: listenhub-ai\nVersion: 0.6.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to the `generate-image.sh` script's capability to auto-install dependencies (`jq`, `curl`) using system package managers (e.g., `sudo apt-get install`) and to write configuration (API key, output directory) directly into the user's shell RC files (`~/.zshrc`, `~/.bashrc`). While these actions are intended for user convenience and configuration, they represent high-risk capabilities that could be exploited if the script or its inputs were compromised, potentially leading to unauthorized command execution or persistence. There is no clear evidence of intentional malicious behavior like data exfiltration or backdoors, but the broad permissions requested for auto-installation and direct modification of shell configuration files elevate the risk beyond benign.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779168168849},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":42,"checkedAt":1789093231482},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill mostly performs cloud media generation, but its image workflow can make unsafe persistent shell changes, auto-install packages with elevated privileges, and send prompts to a differently branded API than the user-facing ListenHub description suggests.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Networked API access and local output files are expected for cloud media generation, but automatic package-manager execution, eval-based command dispatch, and modification of shell startup files are disproportionate for an image-generation wrapper.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact does not have a separate installer, but generate-image.sh performs first-run setup that can auto-install jq or curl through platform package managers, including sudo-based Linux commands, during ordinary use.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill uses broad auto-detection phrases such as explain, draw, and read aloud, and it does not require explicit confirmation before sending user text, URLs, prompts, or reference image URLs to external APIs.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"generate-image.sh writes LISTENHUB_API_KEY and LISTENHUB_OUTPUT_DIR into shell startup files without shell-safe serialization, and lib.sh/generate-image.sh later read shell rc files to recover those values; no service, scheduled task, or backdoor persistence was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Podcast, explainer, TTS, speech, status, and image scripts are present and broadly match the advertised media-generation purpose, but image generation is implemented as a Labnana/Marswave API call while the skill presents the service as ListenHub.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review carefully before installing. Avoid submitting sensitive text, private URLs, confidential prompts, or reference images unless you are comfortable sending them to the disclosed external services. Preinstall curl and jq yourself, set LISTENHUB_API_KEY through OpenClaw environment configuration rather than letting scripts write shell rc files, and treat the image script as higher risk until its Labnana/Marswave provider use, auto-install behavior, and credential persistence are corrected.","findings":"[TP4] expected: Mostly downgraded: the full artifact contains separate scripts for the advertised podcast, explainer, TTS, speech, and image workflows, so the broad capability claim is largely supported; the Labnana/Marswave provider mismatch remains a disclosure concern.\n[AE1] unexpected: Overridden for this adjudication: scripts/generate-image.sh is present in the workspace and was inspected directly.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Accepted for dependency handling: generate-image.sh automatically runs package-manager commands for jq/curl and executes the constructed command with eval, including sudo paths on Linux.\n[TM2] unexpected: Accepted as part of the same auto-install path: apt-based systems run a chained sudo apt-get update and sudo apt-get install command without a separate approval gate.\n[TM1] unexpected: Accepted as part of the same auto-install path: pacman uses --noconfirm, which removes a normal review checkpoint for host modification.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Accepted for persistence: generate-image.sh prompts for an API key and output directory, then writes them into shell startup files, which is persistent and under-disclosed.\n[PE3] expected: Downgraded: the code targets only LISTENHUB_API_KEY and LISTENHUB_OUTPUT_DIR in shell rc files, not unrelated credential stores, but implicit credential discovery is still a scoping concern.\n[LP3] expected: Shell execution and network calls are expected for these wrapper scripts, but the skill does not define narrow permission boundaries or clear confirmation rules for remote submission.\n[RA2] expected: Cloud-generated episodes, images, links, and status IDs are expected for the stated purpose, but retention and deletion expectations are not explained.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: Accepted: trigger phrases such as explain, introduce, and draw are broad enough to route ordinary user requests into external API workflows.\n[SQP-2] expected: External transmission of content is expected for cloud media generation, but the skill lacks a clear privacy warning before sending arbitrary text, URLs, prompts, and reference image URLs.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: Accepted for image generation: the script posts to api.labnana.com while the skill description frames the provider as ListenHub, reducing informed consent.\n[E1] expected: External API transmission is purpose-aligned, but it becomes a concern in the image path because the endpoint/provider differs from the user-facing service description.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted: generate-image.sh writes unescaped user-provided values into shell startup files, creating persistent shell startup command-injection risk and plaintext credential storage.\n[T05] unexpected: Accepted for automatic privileged package installation; downgraded for credential discovery because only the named ListenHub variables are extracted, not broad unrelated credentials.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789093231482}}}}}